1
00:00:15,003 --> 00:00:15,963
你見到呢個tray？

2
00:00:16,003 --> 00:00:18,163
我係自己整嘅

3
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,790
You're an
unfamiliar face

4
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:35,030
Get yourself a
permit if you're looking to do business here

5
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:37,590
Last thing I need
is an unlicensed hooker

6
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:40,189
Can't make as
much cash when you're legal

7
00:00:41,149 --> 00:00:41,669
Yeah

8
00:00:41,709 --> 00:00:43,149
good luck
with that

9
00:00:44,589 --> 00:00:46,069
I just need
permission from him

10
00:00:46,109 --> 00:00:47,069
don't I？

11
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:49,028
Let me meet him

12
00:00:49,188 --> 00:00:49,828
Sorry

13
00:00:49,868 --> 00:00:52,308
I got no idea
who you mean

14
00:00:52,348 --> 00:00:54,868
I'll keep coming
back until I meet him

15
00:00:56,464 --> 00:00:59,592
Until I
meet the baby

16
00:02:35,717 --> 00:02:37,757
You can't catch
the ball with your hands like that

17
00:02:37,797 --> 00:02:39,077
You're not
the goalkeeper

18
00:02:39,117 --> 00:02:40,158
Quit your whining

19
00:02:40,198 --> 00:02:42,198
who died and
made you repp？

20
00:02:42,838 --> 00:02:44,798
Where the hell
did Dugout go？

21
00:02:44,838 --> 00:02:46,078
Where'd Hugo？

22
00:02:46,118 --> 00:02:48,278
Tenma，dummy，Tenma

23
00:02:48,438 --> 00:02:50,358
He told me to
stay with you for a while

24
00:02:50,398 --> 00:02:52,358
Cause he found
the man he was looking for

25
00:02:52,398 --> 00:02:53,438
That's all

26
00:02:53,478 --> 00:02:53,999
That's all

27
00:02:54,039 --> 00:02:57,080
Who leaves a kid
with someone like me？

28
00:02:57,801 --> 00:02:59,082
No way in hell

29
00:02:59,122 --> 00:03:00,122
Thanks a lot，Tema

30
00:03:00,162 --> 00:03:01,723
I have to babysit

31
00:03:01,763 --> 00:03:03,044
I hate kids

32
00:03:03,084 --> 00:03:04,805
First he drops
off the face of the earth

33
00:03:04,845 --> 00:03:07,446
And then he
saddles me with some random brat

34
00:03:07,566 --> 00:03:09,127
Me and him
had an agreement

35
00:03:09,167 --> 00:03:11,088
Doesn't that mean
nothing anymore？

36
00:03:11,128 --> 00:03:14,329
What the hell kind of doctor doesn't want to make some easy money？

37
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:15,370
Here

38
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:17,651
Hey，nice header

39
00:03:17,691 --> 00:03:19,011
Son of a…

40
00:03:19,372 --> 00:03:21,252
Did I look like I
was ready to you？

41
00:03:21,292 --> 00:03:22,093
Hey

42
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:23,173
remember
what I said

43
00:03:23,213 --> 00:03:24,413
you can't
use your hands

44
00:03:24,453 --> 00:03:25,934
That's a
yellow card

45
00:03:25,974 --> 00:03:27,415
I'm throwing
this into traffic

46
00:03:27,455 --> 00:03:29,295
If you mention
the rules one more time

47
00:03:29,335 --> 00:03:30,656
You keep
talking like that

48
00:03:30,696 --> 00:03:31,616
you'll get
a red card

49
00:03:31,656 --> 00:03:33,016
Shut up

50
00:04:10,104 --> 00:04:11,905
Why the hell
are you so late？

51
00:04:12,065 --> 00:04:13,986
Hurry up and
give me the stuff

52
00:04:15,668 --> 00:04:17,389
Give me
the stuff now

53
00:04:20,573 --> 00:04:21,773
Long time no see

54
00:04:21,813 --> 00:04:23,493
Detective Messner

55
00:04:23,893 --> 00:04:24,973
Doctor Tanma？

56
00:04:25,013 --> 00:04:25,653
But…

57
00:04:25,693 --> 00:04:26,573
That's right

58
00:04:26,613 --> 00:04:29,694
That's exactly
what you called me back when we first met

59
00:04:29,734 --> 00:04:33,494
Before I even got
around to telling you what my occupation was

60
00:04:33,694 --> 00:04:35,534
But that was a
long time ago

61
00:04:35,574 --> 00:04:37,655
My days in
medicine are over

62
00:04:38,335 --> 00:04:41,535
But I suppose you'
re no longer a detective

63
00:04:41,735 --> 00:04:44,815
Detective suspended on narcotics charges

64
00:04:45,687 --> 00:04:49,851
This article really came as a shock when I read it six months ago

65
00:04:51,813 --> 00:04:54,094
Don't even think
about running away

66
00:04:54,896 --> 00:04:57,698
I have a gun
trained on you under my jacket

67
00:05:02,022 --> 00:05:04,103
Alright，what do
you want with me？

68
00:05:04,224 --> 00:05:05,385
I need answers

69
00:05:05,425 --> 00:05:08,227
what happened in
Heidelberg almost a year ago

70
00:05:08,348 --> 00:05:09,669
And who was
behind it all？

71
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:12,431
Who ordered you
to do such a terrible thing？

72
00:05:13,527 --> 00:05:15,650
I…I don't
know anything

73
00:05:15,771 --> 00:05:19,457
You killed the
Fordners and Mr， Mower from the post

74
00:05:19,739 --> 00:05:21,342
It wasn't me
that did it

75
00:05:21,382 --> 00:05:22,624
I was hired
as the lookout

76
00:05:22,664 --> 00:05:23,586
that's all

77
00:05:23,626 --> 00:05:24,508
My partner Mueller

78
00:05:24,548 --> 00:05:25,149
he did it

79
00:05:25,189 --> 00:05:26,751
he killed
all of them

80
00:05:28,468 --> 00:05:32,031
Detective Mueller
also left the force soon after the murders

81
00:05:32,071 --> 00:05:33,752
Yeah，he did

82
00:05:33,913 --> 00:05:35,475
I hear that he'
s very well off

83
00:05:35,515 --> 00:05:37,917
Turns out he's
doing good with his money

84
00:05:37,957 --> 00:05:39,159
You，on the
other hand

85
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:41,962
ended up wasting
all of your money on your drug habit

86
00:05:42,002 --> 00:05:43,403
That sound
about right？

87
00:05:43,443 --> 00:05:45,205
He was the one
who took on the job

88
00:05:45,245 --> 00:05:47,087
And he was the
one who committed the murders

89
00:05:47,127 --> 00:05:49,970
He ended up getting the largest portion of the reward

90
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,732
They even tried
to get rid of me

91
00:05:51,772 --> 00:05:54,734
They tried to kill me to make sure I didn't go to the cops

92
00:05:55,634 --> 00:05:57,676
I'm surprised you'
re still breathing

93
00:05:57,716 --> 00:06:00,317
It was the
organisation that helped me

94
00:06:00,798 --> 00:06:02,238
Organisation？

95
00:06:02,479 --> 00:06:03,280
Enough

96
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:05,921
I already told
her too much as it is

97
00:06:07,042 --> 00:06:08,162
Told her？

98
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:09,203
Her who？

99
00:06:10,004 --> 00:06:11,725
Leave me alone
already，I can't…

100
00:06:11,765 --> 00:06:14,367
I can't deal
with you right now

101
00:06:15,008 --> 00:06:17,169
Looks like you're
going through withdrawal

102
00:06:17,249 --> 00:06:18,610
And with me
sitting here

103
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:20,731
no dealer would
come within 20 feet of you

104
00:06:20,771 --> 00:06:23,013
So I suggest
you start talking

105
00:06:24,374 --> 00:06:25,054
I…

106
00:06:25,094 --> 00:06:26,054
I was…

107
00:06:26,415 --> 00:06:28,655
I was saved
by the baby

108
00:06:30,456 --> 00:06:31,697
The baby？

109
00:06:31,897 --> 00:06:33,578
Go to a pub
called Candy

110
00:06:33,618 --> 00:06:35,499
you can find
him there，Wait

111
00:06:35,539 --> 00:06:37,780
who's this baby
you're talking about？

112
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,981
He's a right
wing extremist

113
00:06:40,021 --> 00:06:44,263
He's also a high
official in two of their major political parties

114
00:06:45,074 --> 00:06:46,436
After the
wall fell

115
00:06:46,476 --> 00:06:50,200
The baby tried to
create a town of only pureblooded Germans

116
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:53,002
But his plan
failed and now he's come back

117
00:06:53,444 --> 00:06:54,725
But why'd
he do it？

118
00:06:54,765 --> 00:06:56,687
Why'd he
bother saving you？

119
00:06:58,249 --> 00:06:59,610
The darkness

120
00:07:01,653 --> 00:07:03,735
After the
Berlin Wall fell

121
00:07:04,016 --> 00:07:06,458
A great
darkness was created

122
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:08,461
A monster…

123
00:07:08,822 --> 00:07:10,783
A monster was born

124
00:07:11,697 --> 00:07:12,939
A monster？

125
00:07:12,979 --> 00:07:13,940
Now leave me alone

126
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:15,784
I've already said
everything to that girl

127
00:07:15,824 --> 00:07:16,825
You understand？

128
00:07:16,865 --> 00:07:18,468
What girl
Messner？

129
00:07:18,508 --> 00:07:21,433
She came for
revenge and pointed a gun at me

130
00:07:21,473 --> 00:07:24,679
She's the daughter of that older couple we murdered

131
00:07:24,719 --> 00:07:26,200
You're
saying Anna？

132
00:07:28,918 --> 00:07:29,838
I mean Nina

133
00:07:29,878 --> 00:07:31,918
Nina Fortner
came to see you then？

134
00:07:31,958 --> 00:07:32,518
The…

135
00:07:32,558 --> 00:07:34,398
the baby said
to me that I…

136
00:07:34,438 --> 00:07:37,197
that I was to
send that girl to him if I ever saw her

137
00:07:37,237 --> 00:07:39,917
or if she ever
showed up around these parts

138
00:07:40,237 --> 00:07:41,317
He said that…

139
00:07:41,357 --> 00:07:43,837
that she's
important to use as bait

140
00:07:46,156 --> 00:07:47,596
He's using her…

141
00:07:47,956 --> 00:07:49,236
as bait？

142
00:07:51,977 --> 00:07:54,098
You don't give up
do ya？

143
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:57,702
You're getting to
be a regular coming back all the time

144
00:07:58,503 --> 00:08:00,745
How about I rent
you for an hour or two

145
00:08:00,785 --> 00:08:02,946
so the night ain'
t a total waste？

146
00:08:03,868 --> 00:08:05,469
You're the one
who said I'd get in trouble

147
00:08:05,509 --> 00:08:07,831
if I did business
without the baby's permission

148
00:08:07,871 --> 00:08:10,514
Well，we got
ourselves a mouthy one

149
00:08:10,554 --> 00:08:11,995
Yeah，not so
clever now

150
00:08:12,035 --> 00:08:12,915
are ya？

151
00:08:16,952 --> 00:08:19,914
Is this the girl
who keeps asking to see the baby？

152
00:08:20,476 --> 00:08:21,516
Yes sir

153
00:08:21,797 --> 00:08:23,879
It seems you're
getting your wish

154
00:08:26,442 --> 00:08:28,123
Don't keep
him waiting

155
00:08:51,938 --> 00:08:53,019
Please wait
right here

156
00:08:53,059 --> 00:08:53,940
Miss

157
00:08:54,822 --> 00:08:56,464
Stand on
that eye motif

158
00:08:56,504 --> 00:08:58,145
if you'd
be so kind

159
00:09:02,791 --> 00:09:03,952
Directly
over the iris

160
00:09:03,992 --> 00:09:04,953
please

161
00:09:05,835 --> 00:09:07,636
Yes，much better

162
00:09:39,109 --> 00:09:39,989
Now tell me

163
00:09:40,029 --> 00:09:41,550
Nina Fortner

164
00:09:41,671 --> 00:09:45,753
Doesn't this song resonate with you right down to the soles of your feet？

165
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:47,674
I have to dance

166
00:09:53,479 --> 00:09:55,320
The baby told me

167
00:09:56,121 --> 00:09:59,162
The day another
Hitler is born to us

168
00:09:59,243 --> 00:10:01,444
Our country
will be saved

169
00:10:02,045 --> 00:10:03,566
The girl will be

170
00:10:03,606 --> 00:10:05,927
the perfect
bait for him

171
00:10:07,122 --> 00:10:08,082
Nina

172
00:10:11,643 --> 00:10:13,723
How is it that
you know my name？

173
00:10:13,763 --> 00:10:15,724
That's the
least of what I know

174
00:10:15,764 --> 00:10:18,565
You've also answered to the name of Anna Liebert

175
00:10:18,605 --> 00:10:21,445
But the former is
just as false as the latter

176
00:10:21,485 --> 00:10:24,446
A rose by any
other name does smell as sweet

177
00:10:24,486 --> 00:10:25,806
But they
call me the baby

178
00:10:25,846 --> 00:10:27,087
so I'm biased

179
00:10:27,127 --> 00:10:29,367
Come on
let's cut the rug a bit

180
00:10:29,567 --> 00:10:32,690
Is it true that
you know where my brother is right now？

181
00:10:33,612 --> 00:10:35,134
Yohan，right？

182
00:10:35,174 --> 00:10:36,736
Good name，yes

183
00:10:36,776 --> 00:10:37,377
You know

184
00:10:37,417 --> 00:10:38,537
don't you？

185
00:10:38,578 --> 00:10:42,982
What are you going to do when you finally have your little family reunion？

186
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:49,390
I'm going to
take him down

187
00:10:49,911 --> 00:10:51,792
You shouldn't
whip that out willy nilly

188
00:10:51,832 --> 00:10:54,193
Miss，Someone's
liable to get hurt

189
00:10:54,233 --> 00:10:55,954
Patience，dear，Why

190
00:10:55,994 --> 00:10:59,756
I'm sure Johann
is searching for you even as we speak

191
00:11:09,712 --> 00:11:11,913
I lived around
here when I was your age

192
00:11:11,953 --> 00:11:14,594
Know this place
like the back of my hand

193
00:11:14,634 --> 00:11:16,715
There's a fellow
who buys antiques

194
00:11:16,755 --> 00:11:18,876
And I sell him
this rug I stumbled across

195
00:11:18,916 --> 00:11:23,879
What do you mean？ Don't you have any money left， Mr Heckle？ Shut your yap already

196
00:11:23,919 --> 00:11:26,720
I'm hawking this
rug so I can get the two of us something to eat

197
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,841
I don't hear you
coming up with…

198
00:11:35,010 --> 00:11:36,449
Son of a…

199
00:11:37,529 --> 00:11:39,888
There goes the
neighbourhood

200
00:11:40,928 --> 00:11:41,608
Mr Heckle

201
00:11:41,648 --> 00:11:42,727
what's wrong？

202
00:11:42,767 --> 00:11:43,927
Turks

203
00:11:43,967 --> 00:11:46,926
This whole area
is full of turks now

204
00:11:48,229 --> 00:11:49,069
Hmm

205
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:52,392
your socalled
heirloom is a fake

206
00:11:52,432 --> 00:11:54,353
Huh？What are
you talking about？

207
00:11:54,393 --> 00:11:54,954
Feel it

208
00:11:54,994 --> 00:11:56,154
handwoven silk

209
00:11:56,194 --> 00:11:58,116
You can't fake
this kind of quality

210
00:11:58,156 --> 00:11:59,477
It's synthetic

211
00:11:59,517 --> 00:12:00,437
Tell you what

212
00:12:00,477 --> 00:12:03,959
I'll give you a
hundred marks for it out of sheer sympathy

213
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,321
More like
sheer chicanery

214
00:12:06,361 --> 00:12:09,523
The German guy who had this place would have given me ten grand

215
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:11,724
Well，you can
take it or leave it

216
00:12:12,365 --> 00:12:16,491
Don't you come crying to me when you realise my rug is the real deal

217
00:12:16,531 --> 00:12:19,574
That one hanging
on the wall is the real deal

218
00:12:19,975 --> 00:12:22,298
It's a
genuine Hetikay rug

219
00:12:22,338 --> 00:12:24,100
There's your
handwoven silk

220
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:26,543
Look at the
detail there in the patterns

221
00:12:26,583 --> 00:12:28,024
It's perfect

222
00:12:29,346 --> 00:12:30,307
150，000 marks

223
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:34,271
You sure got
took for a ride

224
00:12:34,311 --> 00:12:36,793
If you really can'
t tell the good stuff from that crap

225
00:12:36,833 --> 00:12:38,554
I feel
sorry for you

226
00:12:38,594 --> 00:12:39,315
We're outta here

227
00:12:39,355 --> 00:12:40,315
Dieder

228
00:12:45,959 --> 00:12:46,600
Hey

229
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,561
I'm getting
kinda hungry

230
00:12:48,761 --> 00:12:50,442
That rug's real

231
00:12:52,075 --> 00:12:54,437
It's a henna cake
just like he said

232
00:12:54,477 --> 00:12:56,357
Only a hundred
and fifty grand？

233
00:12:56,397 --> 00:12:59,599
I could get eight
hundred thousand for a rug as fancy as that

234
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:00,119
Come on

235
00:13:00,159 --> 00:13:01,840
let's get
something to eat already

236
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:02,920
Shut up

237
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,921
If I can get my
hands on that rug

238
00:13:04,961 --> 00:13:07,402
We'll be able to
eat anything we want

239
00:13:07,802 --> 00:13:09,323
How you
gonna do that？

240
00:13:09,363 --> 00:13:10,963
What are you
talking about？

241
00:13:12,204 --> 00:13:14,085
I'm sure I'll
think of something

242
00:13:14,125 --> 00:13:14,925
huh？

243
00:13:15,650 --> 00:13:17,369
Don't
gimme that look

244
00:13:17,409 --> 00:13:18,049
You're hungry

245
00:13:18,089 --> 00:13:18,649
aint you？

246
00:13:18,689 --> 00:13:19,809
Whatever，thief

247
00:13:19,849 --> 00:13:20,449
What？

248
00:13:20,489 --> 00:13:22,249
Put a sock in
it ya little brat

249
00:13:22,289 --> 00:13:23,489
Geez

250
00:13:30,928 --> 00:13:31,888
Hold on a second

251
00:13:31,928 --> 00:13:33,688
Where do you
think you're going？

252
00:13:33,808 --> 00:13:34,407
Sorry

253
00:13:34,447 --> 00:13:36,207
but I'm not
looking to buy

254
00:13:36,247 --> 00:13:37,650
That's not
what I meant

255
00:13:37,690 --> 00:13:38,612
Are you crazy？

256
00:13:38,652 --> 00:13:42,219
An Asian like you is gonna get killed if you walk into a place like that

257
00:13:42,259 --> 00:13:44,744
They don't take
kindly to foreigners in there

258
00:13:44,784 --> 00:13:45,706
But you're Turkish

259
00:13:45,746 --> 00:13:46,588
aren't you？

260
00:13:46,628 --> 00:13:49,473
Is it alright for
you to be doing business around here？

261
00:13:49,513 --> 00:13:50,953
What are
you stupid？

262
00:13:50,993 --> 00:13:53,434
I wouldn't do
business in a dump like this

263
00:13:53,794 --> 00:13:57,555
A friend of mine was just abducted by a bunch of guys who are regulars there

264
00:13:57,595 --> 00:13:58,275
What？

265
00:13:58,315 --> 00:14:01,355
It seems like she
found out a secret of theirs

266
00:14:01,396 --> 00:14:02,516
A secret？

267
00:14:02,556 --> 00:14:03,916
I don't know
what it's all about

268
00:14:03,956 --> 00:14:06,357
But I have to
find her before something bad happens

269
00:14:06,397 --> 00:14:08,477
Who knows what
they're going to do to her？

270
00:14:09,118 --> 00:14:11,003
A woman I know
is in there too

271
00:14:11,043 --> 00:14:12,566
I have to
get her out

272
00:14:12,608 --> 00:14:13,611
Who is she？

273
00:14:13,651 --> 00:14:14,895
What does this
woman look like？

274
00:14:14,935 --> 00:14:16,820
Does she have
long blonde hair？

275
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:17,981
Don't know

276
00:14:18,144 --> 00:14:20,510
I couldn't tell
you what she looks like now

277
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:23,591
Because they just
took a young blonde girl away in a car

278
00:14:24,111 --> 00:14:25,231
Where'd
they take her？

279
00:14:25,271 --> 00:14:26,672
Hey，how
should I know？

280
00:14:26,712 --> 00:14:27,792
But the baby
was with them

281
00:14:27,832 --> 00:14:29,592
so they probably
went to his mansion

282
00:14:29,632 --> 00:14:30,592
The baby？

283
00:14:30,632 --> 00:14:31,633
What kind of car？

284
00:14:31,673 --> 00:14:33,113
What
colour was it？

285
00:14:33,513 --> 00:14:34,433
It was big and red

286
00:14:34,473 --> 00:14:35,473
I don't know

287
00:14:35,513 --> 00:14:36,274
Alright then

288
00:14:36,314 --> 00:14:39,594
I've gotta track
down that red car before it's too late

289
00:14:39,714 --> 00:14:40,434
Wait

290
00:14:40,474 --> 00:14:42,675
you have to do
something to help my friend too

291
00:14:42,715 --> 00:14:43,555
Please help her

292
00:14:43,595 --> 00:14:44,875
she has a
small baby

293
00:14:44,915 --> 00:14:46,836
If something
happens to her…

294
00:14:46,996 --> 00:14:48,116
Please

295
00:15:06,761 --> 00:15:08,082
You're
still alive？

296
00:15:08,122 --> 00:15:10,163
This is my
lucky day

297
00:15:12,005 --> 00:15:13,446
This way please

298
00:15:14,447 --> 00:15:15,448
Without your gun

299
00:15:15,488 --> 00:15:16,208
on this point

300
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:18,249
I'm afraid I
must insist

301
00:15:22,010 --> 00:15:24,132
Thank you for
your cooperation

302
00:15:32,904 --> 00:15:35,186
Go ahead and sit
wherever you like

303
00:15:43,598 --> 00:15:45,160
So the baby
brought you in， eh？

304
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:48,603
Eyes forward
let me see your face

305
00:15:50,691 --> 00:15:51,691
Goodness

306
00:15:51,731 --> 00:15:54,652
But I should have
known you'd be quite a beauty

307
00:15:54,733 --> 00:15:55,253
After all

308
00:15:55,293 --> 00:15:57,974
you are Johann'
s twin sister

309
00:16:08,508 --> 00:16:10,908
My name is
Professor Giedlitz

310
00:16:10,948 --> 00:16:15,227
And the man standing next to Johann in the picture is General Wolff

311
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:17,426
We created
this organisation

312
00:16:17,466 --> 00:16:21,065
along with a pair
of other likeminded individuals

313
00:16:21,425 --> 00:16:23,025
Where are
my manners？

314
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,624
Would you care
for some fruit？

315
00:16:24,664 --> 00:16:25,824
No，thank you

316
00:16:25,864 --> 00:16:27,624
I want to
see Johann

317
00:16:27,823 --> 00:16:29,543
And see
him you will

318
00:16:29,783 --> 00:16:31,063
Once he knows
that you're here

319
00:16:31,103 --> 00:16:33,822
no force on earth
could keep him away

320
00:16:33,862 --> 00:16:36,661
The boy suffers
mightily in your absence

321
00:16:36,701 --> 00:16:38,981
You people don't
know where Johann is either

322
00:16:39,021 --> 00:16:39,900
do you？

323
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:41,260
We need him

324
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:44,020
His country needs him

325
00:16:44,259 --> 00:16:47,899
We four shall
help him fulfil his destiny

326
00:16:50,958 --> 00:16:55,042
Do you have any
idea how Hitler became possessed of such power？

327
00:16:55,323 --> 00:16:58,487
It's because he
saw the three things a person would have to do

328
00:16:58,527 --> 00:17:00,729
to gain
control of a country

329
00:17:05,496 --> 00:17:06,977
Manipulate
the banks

330
00:17:07,017 --> 00:17:08,139
feed the
war machine

331
00:17:08,179 --> 00:17:10,621
and take command
of the military

332
00:17:11,182 --> 00:17:14,586
I'm sure Johann's
working on one of those things right now

333
00:17:16,743 --> 00:17:17,744
Or two

334
00:17:17,905 --> 00:17:19,306
really it's a
question of if

335
00:17:19,346 --> 00:17:20,107
not when

336
00:17:20,147 --> 00:17:22,470
What exactly do
you plan to do with Johann？

337
00:17:22,510 --> 00:17:23,431
Think of it

338
00:17:23,471 --> 00:17:28,276
Hitler bent a weakened nation to his will using nothing but raw charisma

339
00:17:28,477 --> 00:17:31,520
All that from a
man who only made corporal

340
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:35,124
A man whom art
school wouldn't deign to let in

341
00:17:35,365 --> 00:17:38,648
His charisma
appeared after he hit his 30s

342
00:17:40,115 --> 00:17:42,640
Not so with
your brother Johan

343
00:17:42,922 --> 00:17:46,048
He was a leader
of men even as a mere boy

344
00:17:46,531 --> 00:17:49,697
Charisma of
messianic proportions

345
00:17:50,725 --> 00:17:52,968
But even Jesus
Christ had help

346
00:17:53,008 --> 00:17:55,451
Consider the
three Magi and John the Baptist

347
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:58,455
Who heralded the
Saviour's arrival into the world

348
00:17:58,495 --> 00:18:01,217
How they readied
the way for His glory

349
00:18:01,378 --> 00:18:01,979
Likewise

350
00:18:02,019 --> 00:18:04,983
the four of us
have been keeping track of Johann's talents

351
00:18:05,023 --> 00:18:07,024
Ever since he
was a little boy

352
00:18:07,265 --> 00:18:07,866
Exciting

353
00:18:07,906 --> 00:18:09,227
wouldn't you say？

354
00:18:09,548 --> 00:18:11,590
What is it that
you want with me？

355
00:18:12,271 --> 00:18:14,671
Please accept
our hospitality

356
00:18:14,871 --> 00:18:17,951
Until Johann comes looking for you at the very least

357
00:18:17,991 --> 00:18:18,551
Actually

358
00:18:18,591 --> 00:18:20,431
I'm afraid I
must insist

359
00:18:20,471 --> 00:18:23,830
You know too much
for us to let you walk away now

360
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:26,910
Don't worry
about that

361
00:18:26,950 --> 00:18:29,150
I came here of
my own volition

362
00:18:29,310 --> 00:18:31,430
I will wait
here for Johann

363
00:18:31,830 --> 00:18:33,110
Then we agree

364
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:35,310
Now then

365
00:18:35,350 --> 00:18:37,470
you should at
least try the fruit

366
00:18:48,222 --> 00:18:50,544
Good，you're
finally awake

367
00:18:51,425 --> 00:18:52,746
Don't look
so worried

368
00:18:52,786 --> 00:18:54,587
we're not
going to hurt you

369
00:18:55,108 --> 00:18:56,989
Not right
away at least

370
00:18:57,349 --> 00:19:00,551
So what brings
you to my little slice of the world？

371
00:19:00,592 --> 00:19:02,433
Dr， Tenma，Wait

372
00:19:02,473 --> 00:19:04,995
how do you
already know what my name is？

373
00:19:06,403 --> 00:19:08,766
Why don't you
leave the questions to me？

374
00:19:08,806 --> 00:19:11,369
Now all you have
to do is answer

375
00:19:11,409 --> 00:19:13,852
Why exactly were
you snooping around？

376
00:19:13,892 --> 00:19:15,494
I know you're
looking for Johann

377
00:19:15,534 --> 00:19:17,297
but I can't
figure out why

378
00:19:17,337 --> 00:19:19,258
Where are you
keeping Nina？

379
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:22,383
I told you to
leave the questions to me

380
00:19:22,423 --> 00:19:23,384
did I not？

381
00:19:23,424 --> 00:19:24,986
What are you
gonna do with her？

382
00:19:25,026 --> 00:19:27,468
Why do you
insist on vexing me？

383
00:19:29,383 --> 00:19:30,784
Nina is our guest

384
00:19:30,824 --> 00:19:34,667
whereas you are just a meddlesome piece of trash to be disposed of

385
00:19:34,707 --> 00:19:35,468
So

386
00:19:35,668 --> 00:19:37,030
is she okay？

387
00:19:37,070 --> 00:19:38,550
At the moment

388
00:19:38,591 --> 00:19:40,953
but that'll
change soon enough

389
00:19:41,073 --> 00:19:43,075
She's determined to kill Johann

390
00:19:43,115 --> 00:19:45,277
and we simply
can't have that

391
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:48,920
Always a shame
when a pretty girl dies before her time

392
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:52,563
You're just using
Nina as bait to draw out Johann？

393
00:19:52,604 --> 00:19:54,405
What are you
planning on doing？

394
00:19:54,445 --> 00:19:56,006
Who the
hell are you？

395
00:19:56,447 --> 00:19:57,648
That is enough

396
00:19:57,688 --> 00:20:01,530
A person of impure race has no right to ask those questions

397
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:03,692
Their souls just
never know their place

398
00:20:03,732 --> 00:20:07,493
Which is why we'
re putting the Turkish quarter to the torch

399
00:20:14,418 --> 00:20:15,659
The whole quarter？

400
00:20:15,699 --> 00:20:16,819
Indeed

401
00:20:17,099 --> 00:20:20,541
The night sky
tomorrow will be a thing of beauty

402
00:20:20,581 --> 00:20:22,862
A fiery cleansing

403
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,975
If I stay here

404
00:20:28,015 --> 00:20:29,908
then I'll
find Johann

405
00:21:10,152 --> 00:21:11,594
Please help

406
00:21:12,718 --> 00:21:13,840
help me

407
00:21:14,924 --> 00:21:16,047
Who…

408
00:21:16,087 --> 00:21:17,328
who are you？

409
00:21:17,370 --> 00:21:18,212
Please

410
00:21:18,252 --> 00:21:19,375
I beg of you

411
00:21:19,415 --> 00:21:20,416
Okay

412
00:21:20,457 --> 00:21:21,781
where are
you right now？

413
00:21:21,821 --> 00:21:23,383
The third floor

414
00:21:26,337 --> 00:21:28,740
It sounds like you
're speaking with an accent

415
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:30,181
Where are
you from？

416
00:21:30,302 --> 00:21:31,702
I'm Turkish

417
00:21:31,783 --> 00:21:32,624
Please

418
00:21:32,664 --> 00:21:33,906
I've got to escape

419
00:21:33,946 --> 00:21:35,627
They're
going to kill me

420
00:21:36,989 --> 00:21:39,592
Have you been
taken prisoner by the people here？

421
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:40,793
Help me

422
00:21:41,114 --> 00:21:41,755
please

423
00:21:41,795 --> 00:21:43,076
I can't

424
00:21:43,156 --> 00:21:44,478
They're
watching me closely

425
00:21:44,518 --> 00:21:46,240
I've got to
stay in here

426
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:47,280
Please

427
00:21:47,321 --> 00:21:48,923
help me escape

428
00:21:48,963 --> 00:21:50,245
I have to
warn the others

429
00:21:50,285 --> 00:21:52,126
or my baby
will die too

430
00:21:55,378 --> 00:21:56,223
Tomorrow night

431
00:21:56,263 --> 00:21:59,477
we celebrate in
honour of Johann's homecoming

432
00:21:59,881 --> 00:22:04,843
Only the members
of the pure master race like us deserve to survive

433
00:22:05,123 --> 00:22:07,884
Everything else
should just burn away

434
00:22:10,205 --> 00:22:12,285
I overheard
them talking

435
00:22:12,485 --> 00:22:15,766
They're going to
burn it all down tomorrow night

436
00:22:15,806 --> 00:22:17,647
They're
going to destroy

437
00:22:17,687 --> 00:22:20,048
The Turkish
part of town

438
00:22:21,808 --> 00:22:22,929
Help me

439
00:22:23,449 --> 00:22:25,089
please help me

